FSA ELITE =E2=80=93 SALES MASTER FRAMEWORK

WHAT THE SCREENSHOTS ARE REALLY SAYING

1) The communication with characters is super weak.

Problem:
The customer does not feel real. Responses are generic and low-stakes.

Fix:
Build characters like opponents, not chatbots.

Each persona must include:
- Goal (what they want)
- Fear (what they are protecting)
- Constraint (budget, time, spouse, credit, past experience)
- Trigger phrases (what sets them off)
- Decision style (fast/slow, logical/emotional)
- Proof needed (what convinces them)

The AI must resist until the user earns progression.

---

2) Elite Level / Score / Time screens

Right now it=E2=80=99s only right or wrong.

Elite training requires 3 scores:
1. Control (Did you lead the process?)
2. Depth (Did you uncover real motive and pain?)
3. Conversion (Did you move them forward?)

Time alone does not create closers.

---

3) Training Tools (Tactical Response, Skill Builder, Role Play, AI Coach)

All tools must feed one backend intelligence system:
- Skill ratings per category
- Weak spot tracking
- Daily prescribed drills
- Progression gates

---

4) Course Expansion Decision

Build the intelligence layer first.

Minimum Intelligence Layer:
- Skill tags per interaction (budget control, discovery, objection
isolation, etc.)
- Scoring rubric
- Adaptive unlocks (must perform to advance)
- Spaced repetition (weak skills resurface daily)

Without intelligence, content is just pages.

---

5) Brand Consistency

Use the FSA shield logo everywhere:
- Favicon
- App icon
- Header mark
- Loading screen
- Share cards

Consistency builds authority.

---

SALES DNA FROM THE MOVIES

Glengarry Glen Ross:
Pressure exposes weak process.
Drill: One-call control (open =E2=86=92 frame =E2=86=92 discovery =E2=86=92=
 next step).

Wolf of Wall Street:
Certainty + repetition + momentum.
Drill: Tonality reps and certainty closes without being pushy.

The Founder:
Systems beat vibes.
Drill: Standardized repeatable sales process.

Pursuit of Happyness:
Calm under pressure.
Drill: Composure close under resistance.

The Goods:
Energy + showmanship.
Drill: Raise emotion, then anchor to logic.

Love & Other Drugs:
Relationship selling.
Drill: Identity-based connection and long-term positioning.

---

THE FSA SALES MASTER SYSTEM

Pillar 1: Frame Control
- Set agenda
- Set next step early
- Stay calm

Pillar 2: Discovery
- Pain
- Impact
- Timeline
- Decision process
- =E2=80=9CWhat happens if you don=E2=80=99t fix this?=E2=80=9D

Pillar 3: Value Build
- Tie features to THEIR pain
- Use proof + story + comparison

Pillar 4: Objections
Identify the root:
- Money
- Trust
- Timing
- Authority

Handle one at a time.

Pillar 5: Close
Not =E2=80=9Cbuy now.=E2=80=9D
Advance to the next commitment:
- Appointment
- Deposit
- Application
- Trade evaluation
- Manager TO

Pillar 6: Post-Close
- Set expectations
- Ask for referral or review

---

ROLE PLAY AI UPGRADE =E2=80=93 PERSONA ENGINE

Each persona must include hidden variables:
- Budget range
- Trade status
- Credit confidence
- Spouse veto
- Patience meter

Customer replies must always include:
- Emotion
- Objection or concern
- New information only revealed if the correct question is asked

Add a patience meter:
Generic responses reduce trust.

Real resistance examples:
- =E2=80=9CThat=E2=80=99s what the last guy said.=E2=80=9D
- =E2=80=9CYou=E2=80=99re not answering my question.=E2=80=9D
- =E2=80=9CSounds like you=E2=80=99re trying to sell me instead of help me.=
=E2=80=9D

Average performance should feel uncomfortable.

---

BOSS LEVEL PERSONAS

A) Budget Brian =E2=80=93 Cheap, defensive, hates dealers
B) Trade Trap Tina =E2=80=93 Upside down trade, embarrassed
C) Payment Patty =E2=80=93 Only cares about monthly payment
D) Authority Alex =E2=80=93 Someone else makes decisions
E) Skeptic Sam =E2=80=93 Research-heavy, distrusts everything

This framework will shift FSA from content-based training to an adaptive
intelligence-based sales combat system.

